{"name":"Periwinkle Tint","hex":"#d3ddd6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"periwinkle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several evergreen plants of the genus Vinca with blue or white flowers. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Similar plants of genus Catharanthus."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of pale bluish purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/periwinkle"},{"term":"tint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slight coloring.","A pale or faint tinge of any color; especially, a variation of a color obtained by adding white (contrast shade)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shade, to color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Periwinkle (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Periwinkle is a color in the blue and violet family. Its name is derived from the lesser periwinkle or myrtle herb which bears flowers of the same color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Vinca_minor_Nashville.jpg/330px-Vinca_minor_Nashville.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Periwinkle_(color)","wikidata":"Q2617229"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone","wikidata":"Q2749750"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/